From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:27:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: j71t: wake from sleep on the Smart Cover
 events

PMIC GPIO lines 0 and 10 are the Smart Cover hall sensors. Their events,
0x30 and 0x3a, latch while the iPad sleeps; list them as wake-only so
that opening the cover wakes the iPad. The polled switches and their
reserved range are unchanged: lines 0 and 10 are already outside
gpio-reserved-ranges.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts
index acb62901e..2a62f0d95 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts
@@ -40,3 +40,8 @@ &pcie0 {
 &usbdev {
 	apple,retain-gadget-in-s2idle;
 };
+
+/* Smart Cover hall sensors (PMIC GPIO 0 and 10): wake-only. */
+&pmu_gpio {
+	apple,wake-events = <0x30 0x3a>;
+};
